---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import explore from '../../assets/pathways/explore.jpg';
import curious from '../../assets/pathways/curious.jpg';
import connect from '../../assets/pathways/connect.jpg';
---
<Base title="Discover"><div class="station-page">
<section class="station-hero station-hero-split"><div class="station-hero-copy"><p class="eyebrow">DISCOVER / FIELD NOTES & STORIES</p><h1>The forest has <em>questions.</em></h1><p class="lead">Strange finds, beautiful fungi, memorable conversations, and the people who make the search worthwhile.</p><div class="station-actions"><a class="station-button" href="#discover-stories">Explore stories ↓</a><a class="station-text-link" href="/investigate/learn/">My path into research →</a></div></div><Image src={explore} alt="Landscape encountered on a field adventure" widths={[500,850]} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw,48vw"/></section>
<section class="station-content mv-case-feature" aria-labelledby="discover-clathrus-title">
<div class="mv-case-feature-copy"><p class="eyebrow">FEATURED FIELD MYSTERY / DISCOVER → LEARN → INVESTIGATE</p>
<h2 id="discover-clathrus-title">Did the devil’s fingers really move?</h2>
<p>A strange red fungus turns up near Kyiv, far from previously documented records. Is it evidence of a recent arrival—or evidence that we weren't looking closely enough? Follow a real published investigation, one question at a time.</p>
<a class="station-button" href="/investigate/case-studies/clathrus-archeri/">Explore the mystery →</a>
<a class="station-text-link" href="/learn/#evidence-journey">First, learn how to question a sighting ↗</a></div>
<figure><img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Clathrus_archeri_100906693.jpg" alt="Bright red branching arms of Clathrus archeri" loading="lazy"/><figcaption>Illustrative photograph, not the Ukrainian study specimen. Matteo Marcandella, <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Clathrus_archeri_100906693.jpg">CC BY 4.0</a>.</figcaption></figure>
</section>
<section class="station-content" id="discover-stories"><div class="station-section-head"><h2>STORIES WORTH FOLLOWING</h2><span>PEOPLE / PLACES / QUESTIONS</span></div><div class="station-editorial-grid">
<a class="station-editorial-card" href="/investigate/learn/#my-inat"><Image src={curious} alt="Close-up of mushroom structures" widths={[300,600]} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw,30vw"/><span class="station-card-body"><small>FIELD TO LAB</small><strong>From an observation to a research question</strong><span>How field notes, sequences, and collaborators change what we think we know.</span><b>Read the story →</b></span></a>
<a class="station-editorial-card" href="/about/"><Image src={connect} alt="Naturalists exploring together" widths={[300,600]} sizes="(max-width:760px) 100vw,30vw"/><span class="station-card-body"><small>PODCASTS & MEDIA</small><strong>People worth listening to</strong><span>Conversations and connections from The MycoGeeky Podcast and beyond.</span><b>Explore media →</b></span></a>
<a class="station-editorial-card" href="/learn/"><span class="station-card-symbol" aria-hidden="true">✳</span><span class="station-card-body"><small>CULTIVATION</small><strong>Grow something. Learn something.</strong><span>Practical mushroom cultivation as a doorway into experimentation and scientific curiosity.</span><b>Explore cultivation →</b></span></a>
</div></section></div></Base>